" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:13:36-07:00","id":1150972,"title":"","content":"My first question would have to be why? Because it very much matters in regards to what their goal is. For the Sabbat, this seemingly has little to nothing to do with their goal. It neither kills Antediluvians nor hurts the Camarilla. Some might be against them as being pseudo-infernalists, technically. As for the Camarilla, it neither strengths the Masquerade in a particular way, nor weakens the Sabbat. As for the Independents like Assamites and Giovanni, it doesn't hit at their ideals either. Setites might view them as agents of an Aeon known as the Wyrm, I guess. They might also see their corruption as a helpful co-op to freeing people from certain bonds when aimed in a way. As for Pentex, Vampires don't really oppose their mission of corruption and profit. It would just cost them money to pursue this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The goals and relevant players are extremely important in determining such a thing. Because if this is just the Camarilla, just the Sabbat, just certain Independents, or all Vampires versus Pentex changes things. To what degree Pentex and Vampires are willing to break the Masquerade as well. I'm leaning towards Vampires, if only because their ability to just try and take over Pentex is a possibility. And while I understand board members, related spirits, BSD's, etc would be considerable contention, I'm not precisely sure how they'd interact with some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T07:45:23-07:00","id":1150999,"title":"","content":"Pentex. And I don't think it'd be close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:00:27-07:00","id":1151008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1150918#post1150918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing happens. Really that's it. Vampires try to coopt Pentex, they succeed. It continues being an evil megacorporation and leading tool of the wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting, however, to think what could happen if these vampires tried to purgue &quot;the infernalism&quot; in Pentex. Since pentex it's &quot;a leading tool of the wyrm&quot;, if vampires aren't going to change Pentex vile practices, it may as well be that the evil spirits would try to reinsert themselves in power possesing or influencing the vampires and their minions in places of authority. Which would be contrary to the effort of purguing said evil spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-19-2017, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:29:06-07:00","id":1151020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1150972#post1150972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first question would have to be why? Because it very much matters in regards to what their goal is. For the Sabbat, this seemingly has little to nothing to do with their goal. It neither kills Antediluvians nor hurts the Camarilla. Some might be against them as being pseudo-infernalists, technically. As for the Camarilla, it neither strengths the Masquerade in a particular way, nor weakens the Sabbat. As for the Independents like Assamites and Giovanni, it doesn't hit at their ideals either. Setites might view them as agents of an Aeon known as the Wyrm, I guess. They might also see their corruption as a helpful co-op to freeing people from certain bonds when aimed in a way. As for Pentex, Vampires don't really oppose their mission of corruption and profit. It would just cost them money to pursue this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> The goals and relevant players are extremely important in determining such a thing. Because if this is just the Camarilla, just the Sabbat, just certain Independents, or all Vampires versus Pentex changes things. To what degree Pentex and Vampires are willing to break the Masquerade as well. I'm leaning towards Vampires, if only because their ability to just try and take over Pentex is a possibility. And while I understand board members, related spirits, BSD's, etc would be considerable contention, I'm not precisely sure how they'd interact with some of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Camarilla, Sabbat and Independents. And they will not attempt to co-opt Pentex. They will bend their every fiber of being to destroy Pentex, even if that means breaching the Masquerade, and vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:57:41-07:00","id":1151030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1151020#post1151020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camarilla, Sabbat and Independents. And they will not attempt to co-opt Pentex. They will bend their every fiber of being to destroy Pentex, even if that means breaching the Masquerade, and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not to be rude, but this doesn't ask the question in my very first sentence, <i>why</i>? How follows why in this. These groups both have goals. If they are going to illogical stop pursuing their goals, kind of a different setting altogether.<br /> <br /> Also, kind of tying Vampires hands a bit that they can't co-opt and no Antediluvians as well. I'd be more willing to push it back to Vampires if the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Independents are working together. Given the general lack of cooperation being a big issue for Kindred.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T23:18:24-07:00","id":1151222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1151030#post1151030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not to be rude, but this doesn't ask the question in my very first sentence, <i>why</i>? How follows why in this. These groups both have goals. If they are going to illogical stop pursuing their goals, kind of a different setting altogether.<br /> <br /> Also, kind of tying Vampires hands a bit that they can't co-opt and no Antediluvians as well. I'd be more willing to push it back to Vampires if the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Independents are working together. Given the general lack of cooperation being a big issue for Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this particular caveat tying Vampires hand at all. Even a single Antediluvian can demolish Pentex. Hands down. And while they will not attempt to co-opt Pentex, they <i>will </i>cooperate to eradicate Pentex from face of the Earth.<br /> <br /> And for reason of cooperation between sects...let's assume vampires somehow discover Pentex endgame and step in to prevent it. To preserve their food source and by extension, their own unlife, At any cost. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T06:43:50-07:00","id":1151290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1151222#post1151222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this particular caveat tying Vampires hand at all. Even a single Antediluvian can demolish Pentex. Hands down. And while they will not attempt to co-opt Pentex, they <i>will </i>cooperate to eradicate Pentex from face of the Earth.<br /> <br /> And for reason of cooperation between sects...let's assume vampires somehow discover Pentex endgame and step in to prevent it. To preserve their food source and by extension, their own unlife, At any cost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pentex's end game is &quot;make money&quot;. There is no End game. Wyrm service is immediately beneficial its not about &quot;Someday We'll rule the world&quot; Pentex already has that. The price is to keep making it shittier. They destroy the world by being the worst aspects of humanity given root. Something Kindred may have trouble seeing as an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T07:30:20-07:00","id":1151310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1151290#post1151290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex's end game is &quot;make money&quot;. There is no End game. Wyrm service is immediately beneficial its not about &quot;Someday We'll rule the world&quot; Pentex already has that. The price is to keep making it shittier. They destroy the world by being the worst aspects of humanity given root. Something Kindred may have trouble seeing as an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, now I understand - Bloodsuckers ARE the physical manifestation of the worst aspects of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T15:58:14-07:00","id":1151497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1151310#post1151310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, now I understand - Bloodsuckers ARE the physical manifestation of the worst aspects of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't say that, I would say the Kindred condition is prone to brining out the worst aspects of people. Its hard to say be charitable when you see someone as food on some level for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T00:38:34-07:00","id":1152424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1151008#post1151008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting, however, to think what could happen if these vampires tried to purgue &quot;the infernalism&quot; in Pentex. Since pentex it's &quot;a leading tool of the wyrm&quot;, if vampires aren't going to change Pentex vile practices, it may as well be that the evil spirits would try to reinsert themselves in power possesing or influencing the vampires and their minions in places of authority. Which would be contrary to the effort of purguing said evil spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't work in the bane's favor. As per WTA Possessed only banes of blood and death can control vamps. Otherwise the vamp gets full control, all the banes powers, and the bane gets zip as the vamp isn't even inclined to feed it. Hilarious as the reactions would be, all you'd get are a few pissed of banes with their hands tied and a small group of super-fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T17:01:12-07:00","id":1152638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152424#post1152424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wouldn't work in the bane's favor. As per WTA Possessed only banes of blood and death can control vamps. Otherwise the vamp gets full control, all the banes powers, and the bane gets zip as the vamp isn't even inclined to feed it. Hilarious as the reactions would be, all you'd get are a few pissed of banes with their hands tied and a small group of super-fomori.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few members on the board are serial killers a la Patrick Bateman who would probably attract a lot of psychomachiae, so it's not inconceivable that the banes that the vampires take on take the vampires for a ride and show them how empty they really are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T21:22:00-07:00","id":1152705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152424#post1152424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wouldn't work in the bane's favor. As per WTA Possessed only banes of blood and death can control vamps. Otherwise the vamp gets full control, all the banes powers, and the bane gets zip as the vamp isn't even inclined to feed it. Hilarious as the reactions would be, all you'd get are a few pissed of banes with their hands tied and a small group of super-fomori.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> w20 has quite afew Banes that can and will mess up vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T04:28:17-07:00","id":1152756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152705#post1152705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">w20 has quite afew Banes that can and will mess up vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in there are more spirits that can possess vampires or their are more spirits of blood or spirits of death? I'd also like to ask for context, as what I was refering to was if a bane tried to &quot;possess a vamps body&quot;, but it sounds like you interpreted what I said as &quot;if a bane fights a vampire&quot;.<br /> <br /> I may be interpreting what you typed wrong though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T04:28:17-07:00","id":1152757,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T05:06:41-07:00","id":1152766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war#post1150912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who will win? Let's assume vampires <i>in </i>Pentex and Sabbat Wyrm-cultists are going to side with Pentex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Kindred Sects would be involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T11:42:31-07:00","id":1152853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152756#post1152756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in there are more spirits that can possess vampires or their are more spirits of blood or spirits of death?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but Scrags all have Rage 10, which means that if a group of them temporarily possesses a bunch of people around the vampire as their method of materialization, they can probably kill the vampire inside of a few seconds. Any bane with sufficiently high stats can threaten Kindred, all the more so because vampires only get Fortitude to soak aggravated damage, which spirits, much like Garou, can deliver inherently in combat. And if a vampire runs afoul of a furmling or an atomic-spirit, you're looking at a high likelihood of said vampire becoming extra-crispy and irradiated (the latter tends to be more of a worry for everyone around the vampire, up until the point the radiation becomes intense enough to set nearby flammable objects on fire).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd also like to ask for context, as what I was refering to was if a bane tried to &quot;possess a vamps body&quot;, but it sounds like you interpreted what I said as &quot;if a bane fights a vampire&quot;.<br /> <br /> I may be interpreting what you typed wrong though. </div> </div> </div>Possession isn't quite as widespread as the number of banes that exist. Some just want to tear shit apart, and the ones that can cross the Gauntlet can be a threat that Kindred never see coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T12:18:13-07:00","id":1152869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possession isn't quite as widespread as the number of banes that exist. Some just want to tear shit apart, and the ones that can cross the Gauntlet can be a threat that Kindred never see coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheas was answering to a post of mine ,where I mentioned banes possessing vampires. In that context he's right, for that to work it would have to be the correct banes (albeit I also mentioned their followers-probably the vampires would try to rule the company via proxy, and these proxies may not have the same resistence).<br /> <br /> Still it's interesting to think on Bane reaction to said takeover. Maybe possesion it's a very specific power that won't be used very often, but Banes will be arround that company if it remains a bastion of the Wyrm, interested in corrupting stuff even more.<br /> <br /> If vampires don't care about Pentex being a bastion of the Wyrm (more than likely since vampires don't care a lot for the spiritual) the Banes would continue their work uninterrupted. Would working in an environment that's even more Bane chocked than the average Tremere Chantry (I would think that because Pentex it's rumored to be the incarnation of the Urge Wyrm of Greed) have any effect on vampires (like they becoming even greedier and less humane)?<br /> What if vampires inside try to make Pentex less of a Wyrm bastion? (maybe they are a powerful group of spiritualist Tremere that don't like Banes, or maybe they are Brujah idealists that want to make Pentex a better place. Granted, this does depart from the thread assumptions about an &quot;all out war&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-25-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T12:45:10-07:00","id":1152879,"title":"","content":"narrwing this down a bit would the sabbat want to do this, they do have an inquisition hellbent on wiping out infernalism and it'd be a pretty easy sell for them to get the rest of the sabbat to want to take over/down a group with that much money and influence in mortal society, partially out of greed and partially to destroy a competitor, i'd mosty side with the sabbat on that fight due to being able to competely blindside pentex in terms of ability and influence (insert nobody expects the sabbat inquisition joke here), mental domination, flesh warping and pretty much everything invlving the abyss would be one heck of a shock to the system (particularly the mind control being used up the chain of command). Ironically the sabbats biggest setback might be that koldunic sorcery will backfire as elemental sorcery is something that pentex MIGHT be prepared for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 10-25-2017, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:39:59-07:00","id":1152915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152879#post1152879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">narrwing this down a bit would the sabbat want to do this, they do have an inquisition hellbent on wiping out infernalism and it'd be a pretty easy sell for them to get the rest of the sabbat to want to take over/down a group with that much money and influence in mortal society, partially out of greed and partially to destroy a competitor, i'd mosty side with the sabbat on that fight due to being able to competely blindside pentex in terms of ability and influence (insert nobody expects the sabbat inquisition joke here), mental domination, flesh warping and pretty much everything invlving the abyss would be one heck of a shock to the system (particularly the mind control being used up the chain of command). Ironically the sabbats biggest setback might be that koldunic sorcery will backfire as elemental sorcery is something that pentex MIGHT be prepared for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also as far as sabbat and camarilla go, the sabbat is the the won that'd actually be willing to risk the masquerade and go to &quot;war&quot; with someone.<br /> <br /> They'd likely need someone to tip them off that pentex is a massive infernalist cult though. The Cam likely couldn't care less (though they'll openly denounce and kill infernalists) and probably own a large chunk of the stocks via proxy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:55:22-07:00","id":1152926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152915#post1152915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also as far as sabbat and camarilla go, the sabbat is the the won that'd actually be willing to risk the masquerade and go to &quot;war&quot; with someone.<br /> <br /> They'd likely need someone to tip them off that pentex is a massive infernalist cult though. The Cam likely couldn't care less (though they'll openly denounce and kill infernalists) and probably own a large chunk of the stocks via proxy</div> </div> </div> </div>actually if pentex can figure out whats happening quickly enough they might be able to use the camarilla as a shield from the sabbat, that could make an interesting sabbat chronicle where the sabbat come across as a more positive force where the camarilla come across like tools of evil the sabbat always paint them as","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T17:30:14-07:00","id":1152983,"title":"","content":"I think this scenario as many other can happen. Let's assume that in a common effort all vampires have to fight Pentex. Maybe Pentex has developed a new weapon to kill vampires, rates of killing with such weapon becomes a problem now they have to do something about it, and very much together - it's a race matter, not such as of a house or clan, much greater problem!<br /> <br /> Or a scenario where Vampires are facing extinction because of something, they will coop to survive.<br /> <br /> Cause, 'hey' let's face it, the machine already won.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YtsZoIe3Czk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YtsZoIe3Czk</a> - a Nuwisha laughs somewhere hehehe<br /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13101-ntrlz","name":"Ntrlz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13101_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T17:44:25-07:00","id":1152986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152869#post1152869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheas was answering to a post of mine ,where I mentioned banes possessing vampires. In that context he's right, for that to work it would have to be the correct banes (albeit I also mentioned their followers-probably the vampires would try to rule the company via proxy, and these proxies may not have the same resistence).<br /> <br /> Still it's interesting to think on Bane reaction to said takeover. Maybe possesion it's a very specific power that won't be used very often, but Banes will be arround that company if it remains a bastion of the Wyrm, interested in corrupting stuff even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reaction of other banes is likely to be on the order of avoiding that tactic in favor of using other, more subtle Charms to direct the behavior of vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If vampires don't care about Pentex being a bastion of the Wyrm (more than likely since vampires don't care a lot for the spiritual) the Banes would continue their work uninterrupted. </div> </div> </div>The world that Pentex helped to shape does have a lot of inertia propelling it in that direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would working in an environment that's even more Bane chocked than the average Tremere Chantry (I would think that because Pentex it's rumored to be the incarnation of the Urge Wyrm of Greed) have any effect on vampires (like they becoming even greedier and less humane)? </div> </div> </div>Banes that see their fellows get trapped in the spiritual roach motels probably learn to use the lack of a vampire's spiritual awareness against it. It hides around, it whispers suggestions in a way that seem oddly well-taken by some part of the vampire (banes with higher degrees of Gnosis will probably notice that there's a side to vampires that's much more amenable to them), and then sits back to watch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if vampires inside try to make Pentex less of a Wyrm bastion? (maybe they are a powerful group of spiritualist Tremere that don't like Banes, or maybe they are Brujah idealists that want to make Pentex a better place. Granted, this does depart from the thread assumptions about an &quot;all out war&quot;) </div> </div> </div>Could a group of vampires other than perhaps some very idealistic Healer Salubri even take a crack at that? Vampires are concerned with securing blood and keeping people distracted from their depredations. Both of these work quite well into Pentex's Byzantine and obscure corporate structure. It's just that you have fewer fomori around and more ghouls waiting to pull a portion of the new hires to the boss's office to become the new herd members. That seems like it would be quite pleasing to most Urge Wyrms, and not really put much of a dent in the interest that Vorus and Relshab would have in it, because it would presumably keep existing and making money to keep existing and making money, only with the additional point of being a huge front for securing a lot of kine for Kindred consumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:13:55-07:00","id":1153003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152986#post1152986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banes that see their fellows get trapped in the spiritual roach motels probably learn to use the lack of a vampire's spiritual awareness against it. It hides around, it whispers suggestions in a way that seem oddly well-taken by some part of the vampire (banes with higher degrees of Gnosis will probably notice that there's a side to vampires that's much more amenable to them), and then sits back to watch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires aren't spiritually dead in the sense they can't interact with it(the lack of Soul/&quot;soul&quot; is irrelevant to that apparently). Any vampire with a dot in auspex and awarness(read every ancillae that wants to survive) is going to notice the evil presence speaking to them after they took over a known infernalist lair. Any vampire with two brain cells to rub together(unfortunately going to be pretty low among neonates) will figure out that this is likely a demon. Whether they run screaming to the tremere for exorcism, pick a fight or try to deal for more power, their experience with the jyhad means that any self respecting vampire is Very Unlikely to be an unwitting pawn in the banes games(unless of course they're a neonate, then they'll be pawns to Both the wyrm and their elders).<br /> <br /> Unless we're talking a straight werwolf game and not a WTA/VTM crossover. A vampire from VTM can out-maneuver/kick the tush of a WTA vampire the same way a WTA Garou would absolutely Destroy a VTM lupine in a straight up fight. As is true of all game lines<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1152986#post1152986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a group of vampires other than perhaps some very idealistic Healer Salubri even take a crack at that? Vampires are concerned with securing blood and keeping people distracted from their depredations. Both of these work quite well into Pentex's Byzantine and obscure corporate structure. It's just that you have fewer fomori around and more ghouls waiting to pull a portion of the new hires to the boss's office to become the new herd members. That seems like it would be quite pleasing to most Urge Wyrms, and not really put much of a dent in the interest that Vorus and Relshab would have in it, because it would presumably keep existing and making money to keep existing and making money, only with the additional point of being a huge front for securing a lot of kine for Kindred consumption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes the tremere could with the way of spirit and the Tzimisce could using koldunism(which is spirit magic anyway). It may not matter either way for the greed incarnae, but the smaller banes will get a kick in the teeth when pentex stops giving them blood sacrifices in favor of using them to feed their new vampire overlords. Pentex itself likely wouldn't even change much save being more eco-friendly minus the infernalism(though it'll still be just as werewolf-unfriendly. The vamprs may try to save the planet to maintain their herds, but they'll still turn a cairn into a parking-lot the first chance thy get.)<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, It'd probably gain some weaver backing. The god of stasis is probably better to have on the companies side than the god of bankruptcy anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:17:46-07:00","id":1153005,"title":"","content":"It's a victory for humanity no matter who wins","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T19:34:31-07:00","id":1153011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrm20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are hard to possess. Perhaps the Curse of<br /> Caine is such a potent form of damnation that any lesser<br /> affliction has trouble taking root; perhaps it has something<br /> to do with vampires already being dead. Whatever<br /> the reason, very few Banes can find any purchase in a<br /> vampire\u2019s pale and withered soul. Those that do tend to<br /> be Banes of blood and madness, and they can make a<br /> vampire\u2019s unlife very short and very unpleasant indeed.<br /> Detailed below are two examples of the kind of fomori<br /> possible when a Bane manages to curl up in the black<br /> and empty pit that was once a vampire\u2019s soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ones that effects vampires are rare but powerful but they REALLY FUCK UP Vampires. So if Pentex has some idea what's happening they can direct things to their advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T20:12:03-07:00","id":1153020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153003#post1153003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires aren't spiritually dead in the sense they can't interact with it(the lack of Soul/&quot;soul&quot; is irrelevant to that apparently). Any vampire with a dot in auspex and awarness(read every ancillae that wants to survive) is going to notice the evil presence speaking to them after they took over a known infernalist lair. Any vampire with two brain cells to rub together(unfortunately going to be pretty low among neonates) will figure out that this is likely a demon. Whether they run screaming to the tremere for exorcism, pick a fight or try to deal for more power, their experience with the jyhad means that any self respecting vampire is Very Unlikely to be an unwitting pawn in the banes games(unless of course they're a neonate, then they'll be pawns to Both the wyrm and their elders).<br /> <br /> Unless we're talking a straight werwolf game and not a WTA/VTM crossover. A vampire from VTM can out-maneuver/kick the tush of a WTA vampire the same way a WTA Garou would absolutely Destroy a VTM lupine in a straight up fight. As is true of all game lines</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred probably have better shakes sensing and dealing with the dead and various astral emanations. The living spirits of the Middle Umbra are not really in their purview, and form a blind spot for most vampires, since the power of the grave offered by blood doesn't play well with Gnosis or Rage, at least as far as we can tell from what sort of shit one is in for as an Abomination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes the tremere could with the way of spirit and the Tzimisce could using koldunism(which is spirit magic anyway). </div> </div> </div>What type of spirits is a key question there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It may not matter either way for the greed incarnae, but the smaller banes will get a kick in the teeth when pentex stops giving them blood sacrifices in favor of using them to feed their new vampire overlords. Pentex itself likely wouldn't even change much save being more eco-friendly minus the infernalism(though it'll still be just as werewolf-unfriendly. The vamprs may try to save the planet to maintain their herds, but they'll still turn a cairn into a parking-lot the first chance thy get.) </div> </div> </div>How would a sprawling, monstrous megacorporation from capitalist hell become more favorable to its surroundings just because vampires kick the prior bosses out and take their place? The vast majority of reasons that Pentex skirts environmental regulations are the same reason that all other corporations do, because they can make more money paying a pittance in fines than they can complying with said regulations. Vampires, particularly the kind that preferentially nest in corporate power structures, have few compelling reasons to stop this, and would likely continue on just as before. Meet the new boss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thinking about it, It'd probably gain some weaver backing. The god of stasis is probably better to have on the companies side than the god of bankruptcy anyway </div> </div> </div>No, vampires are still more Wyrm than Weaver. It takes an awfully long time for any correspondence with the latter to show up (centuries to millennia), but the former is there from the beginning. You can tell because performing a rite of cleansing on one causes it pain, but the taint remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T21:14:30-07:00","id":1153043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153020#post1153020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred probably have better shakes sensing and dealing with the dead and various astral emanations. The living spirits of the Middle Umbra are not really in their purview, and form a blind spot for most vampires, since the power of the grave offered by blood doesn't play well with Gnosis or Rage, at least as far as we can tell from what sort of shit one is in for as an Abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless we're talking necromancy I don't think disciplines exclude any type of spirit, in fact auspex doesn't call out any creature spirit or otherwise as being able to avoid it without a gift like blur of the milky eye(which there are rules for which would win).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153020#post1153020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What type of spirits is a key question there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It calls out spirits of the earth, so I assume they'd be middle umbral. If not specifically, then I'd assume it works on any &quot;spirits of the earth&quot; which would be any of the animistic spirits. Also path of spirit directly talks about affecting spirits of the umbra, not just the low umbra. I'd rather not impose rules on a splat unless they're called out in the books, Otherwise that's your own house rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153020#post1153020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a sprawling, monstrous megacorporation from capitalist hell become more favorable to its surroundings just because vampires kick the prior bosses out and take their place? The vast majority of reasons that Pentex skirts environmental regulations are the same reason that all other corporations do, because they can make more money paying a pittance in fines than they can complying with said regulations. Vampires, particularly the kind that preferentially nest in corporate power structures, have few compelling reasons to stop this, and would likely continue on just as before. Meet the new boss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I would however think many kindred are like humans and panic over threats we don't completely understand. One elder from when men were still hunters might be want to preserve the wildlife in memory of the &quot;Glory Days&quot;, another might be from the industial revolution remembering how an accident killed his crops, and another might have been an aristocrat in those times, blatently destroying forests to afford a new yacht to sink.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153020#post1153020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, vampires are still more Wyrm than Weaver. It takes an awfully long time for any correspondence with the latter to show up (centuries to millennia), but the former is there from the beginning. You can tell because performing a rite of cleansing on one causes it pain, but the taint remains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the vampires taking over pentex won't be freshly embraced neonate that smell like fresh wyrm dung, the ones doing the heavy lifting(read buying the stock and dominating/presence/blood bonding the employees) will be old enough to smell like the tomb dust of the weaver as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T23:02:37-07:00","id":1153069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153043#post1153043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless we're talking necromancy I don't think disciplines exclude any type of spirit, in fact auspex doesn't call out any creature spirit or otherwise as being able to avoid it without a gift like blur of the milky eye(which there are rules for which would win).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It calls out spirits of the earth, so I assume they'd be middle umbral. If not specifically, then I'd assume it works on any &quot;spirits of the earth&quot; which would be any of the animistic spirits. Also path of spirit directly talks about affecting spirits of the umbra, not just the low umbra. I'd rather not impose rules on a splat unless they're called out in the books, Otherwise that's your own house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's the word of the W:tA Revised Storyteller's Handbook and some inferences from how Vampire and Demon sync up in setting. Note that the Middle Umbra is completely ignored by the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, I would however think many kindred are like humans and panic over threats we don't completely understand. One elder from when men were still hunters might be want to preserve the wildlife in memory of the &quot;Glory Days&quot;, another might be from the industial revolution remembering how an accident killed his crops, and another might have been an aristocrat in those times, blatently destroying forests to afford a new yacht to sink. </div> </div> </div>Elders are not known for having sympathetic or generous outlooks on existence, though, nor are they keen to share if they don't have to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I imagine the vampires taking over pentex won't be freshly embraced neonate that smell like fresh wyrm dung, the ones doing the heavy lifting(read buying the stock and dominating/presence/blood bonding the employees) will be old enough to smell like the tomb dust of the weaver as well. </div> </div> </div>Treating employees like a blood bank is going to make the entire operation rather corruptive. Also, even if they ping on Sense Weaver, they'll still ping on Sense Wyrm as well. They're corruption stuffed into little-changing shell, so neither is one that they're going to be escaping. At least, not if they're the type interested in gaining and maintaining societal influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T01:05:58-07:00","id":1153086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153069#post1153069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's the word of the W:tA Revised Storyteller's Handbook and some <b>inferences</b> from how Vampire and Demon sync up in setting. Note that the Middle Umbra is completely ignored by the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to point out that said book mentions the astral plane used in the Astral Projection power of Auspex and Nothing Else. If you want to rule that vampires only interact with the dark/low umbra that's fine, but it is your own house-rule not universal to all games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153069#post1153069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elders are not known for having sympathetic or generous outlooks on existence, though, nor are they keen to share if they don't have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't generalize all elders to the same behavior as that limits potential npc character options for them, I believe elders are even described as horribly nostalgic and resistant to change, but I'll consign that many elders likely don't care one way or the other about pentex's practices as long as they make money","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T01:10:27-07:00","id":1153087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1150912-pentex-vs-vampires-all-out-war?p=1153086#post1153086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like to point out that said book mentions the astral plane used in the Astral Projection power of Auspex and Nothing Else. If you want to rule that vampires only interact with the dark/low umbra that's fine, but it is your own house-rule not universal to all games.</div> </div> </div> </div>And more recent books that is to say Umbra 20 say that the astral plane is part of the High umbra and werewolves have difficulty interacting with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}